ews\nEvents\nResearch\nAtomic, Molecular, and Optical\nBiological Physics\nCondensed Matter\nGravity & Cosmology\nParticles & Fields\nParticle Astrophysics\nPhysics Education Research\nMachine Shop\nSafety\nCommunity\nAPS-IDEA\nDialogues\nFeedback\nGuide Program\nMentoring\nResources\nSubmitted by cvb6133\non Wed, 03/20/2019 - 13:57\nGraduate\nApplying to\nPenn State\nBreadcrumb\nDepartment of Physics\nPhysics Graduate\nPhysics Applying to Penn State\nphysics\nAbout\nAlumni and Giving\nResources for Postdocs\nJoin Us\nContact us\nGraduate\nGraduate Life\nApplying to Penn State\nAdmissions Frequently Asked Questions\nGraduate Courses\nGraduate Handbook and Degree Requirements\nGraduate Awards\nQualifying Exams\nEquity and Inclusion, Academic Integrity\nGraduate Placement\nUndergraduate\nCourses\nDegree Information\nAwards\nResearch\nSociety of Physics Students\nSchreyers Honors College students in physics\nStudent Resources\nLearning Assistants\nTake a Professor for Lunch\nPeople\nFaculty\nGraduate Faculty\nGraduate Students\nPostdoctoral Researcher\nStaff\nNews\nEvents\nResearch\nAtomic, Molecular, and Optical\nBiological Physics\nCondensed Matter\nGravity & Cosmology\nParticles & Fields\nParticle Astrophysics\nPhysics Education Research\nMachine Shop\nSafety\nCommunity\nAPS-IDEA\nDialogues\nFeedback\nGuide Program\nMentoring\nResources\ngraduate\nGraduate Life\nResearch\nSetting\nRecreation\nHousing\nFinances\nStudent Groups\nComments\nApplying to Penn State\nAdmissions Frequently Asked Questions\nGraduate Courses\nGraduate Handbook and Degree Requirements\nGraduate Awards\nPhysics Student Research Awards\nStudent Teaching Awards\nOther Graduate Awards\nQualifying Exams\nEquity and Inclusion, Academic Integrity\nGraduate Placement\nThanks for your interest in the Penn State graduate program in Physics. Admission to our graduate program is granted jointly by the Penn State Fox Graduate School and the Department of Physics.\nTo apply, please complete a formal online application through the Penn State Fox Graduate School. The application is due on Jan 15 for the incoming class of the year. Note that there is an application fee payable to the Fox Graduate School. To ensure access to all qualified applicants, the Physics PhD program is waiving the fee for ALL applicants this year. There is no cost to apply. Please enter the waiver code PHYS2027 in your application.\nWe will begin accepting applications for the Fall 2027 academic year starting on October 1, 2026.\nThe Fox Graduate School application process will ask for the following materials listed below. The online application process will also give you an opportunity to provide additional optional information that can be useful to the admissions committee.\nA copy of your official undergraduate transcript. Documents should not contain Social Security numbers or any other individually identifying numbers.\nA copy of your official graduate transcript (if any). Documents should not contain Social Security numbers or any other individually identifying numbers.\nThe names and contact information for three references.\nBrief written answers to four questions regarding your academic preparation, research experience, fit in our program, and personal qualities. Please refer to the detailed prompts in the application portal.\nThe names of up to 3 Graduate Faculty from our department with whom you are interested in working and up to 3 subfields of your interest.\nInternational applicants from non-English speaking countries are required to submit results of the Test of English as a Foreign Language (TOEFL), or the International English Language Testing System (IELTS) electronically to Penn State. To submit your scores, please use the institution code 2660 for the TOEFL and search Penn State Graduate School for IELTS. If you need to submit hard copy score reports they should be sent directly from your testing agency to Penn State's Graduate School at the following address:\nThe Pennsylvania State University\nGraduate Enrollment Services\n114 Kern Building\nUniversity Park, PA 16802\nPlease read our FAQs, where you will find answers to most questions we receive from applicants. If you have read all the FAQs and are unable to find the answer to your question, you may write to gradapps@lists.psu.edu.\nFrequently Asked Questions.\nWelcome to Penn State Brochure\nCollege Resources\nAdministrative Offices\nCommunications\nData Services\nEmployment Opportunities\nFacilities\nCollege Resources 2\nFinance\nHuman Resources\nInformation Technology\nInstruction and Curricula\nResearch Administration\nResources\nOffices and Centers\nGrove Center for Excellence in Science Education\nOffice for Undergraduate Students\nOffice of Development and Alumni Relations\nOffice of Diversity and Inclusion\nOffice of Science Engagement\nOffice of Science Outreach\nStudent Programs\nAcademic Advising\nCo-op\nEducation Abroad\nInternship\nUndergraduate Research\nPennState-Eberly College of Science\nFooter Menu\nCollege Org. Chart\nHotline\nContact Us\nLog in\nFollow the Eberly College of Science\nCopyright \u00a9 , The Pennsylvania State University | Privacy and Legal Statements", "links": [["Skip to main content", "https://science.psu.edu/physics/graduate/applying#main-content"], ["News", "https://science.psu.edu/news"], ["Events", "https://science.psu.edu/events"], ["Development and Alumni Relations", "https://science.psu.edu/alumni-and-development"], ["Faculty and Staff Directory", "https://science.psu.edu/people"], ["", "https://science.psu.edu/"], ["News", "https://science.psu.edu/news"], ["Events", "https://science.psu.edu/events"], ["Development and Alumni Relations", "https://science.psu.edu/alumni-and-development"], ["Faculty and Staff Directory", "https://science.psu.edu/people"], ["About", "https://science.psu.edu/physics"], ["Alumni and Giving", "https://science.psu.edu/physics/alumni-and-giving"], ["Resources for Postdocs", "https://science.psu.edu/physics/resources-